course: dictionary
lesson: 5596
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lid has two main meanings. The first is a cover on top of a box, pot, jar or bin that you can lift or take off. «Glue sticks dry out if left open, so the lid or cap always goes back on.»
explain: The second meaning is an eyelid: the skin that closes over your eye. People often just say lid for this. «The dog's eyes moved under the lids while it dreamed.»
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. A pot or a bin has a lid, while an eye has lids. Ask yourself what is being talked about, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Lid is also used in phrases. «Put a lid on it» means be quiet or stop it, «keep a lid on» means keep under control or secret, and «flip your lid» means get very angry. In these phrases, the word is not about a cover at all.
fact: A lid is a cover on top of a box, pot, jar or bin.
fact: An eyelid is the skin that closes over your eye.
fact: A lid keeps heat and steam in, so water boils faster.
fact: In a fire, a lid takes away oxygen, so the fire can go out. Never use water on a fire in a pan.
fact: «Flip your lid» means get very angry.
exercise: «The dog's eyes moved under the lids while it dreamed.» What is a lid in this sentence? | A cap on a bottle | *An eyelid, the skin that closes over an eye | A cover on top of a pot | A lid on a bin
exercise: «If a hot pan catches fire, what should you do?» | *Put a lid on it | Pour oil on it | Throw water on it | Carry the pan outside quickly
exercise: Dad shouts, «Don't flip your lid!» What does flip your lid mean? | Fall fast asleep | Do a backflip | Take the lid off a pan | *Get very angry
test: «Keep a lid on it, please, until the news is out.» What does keep a lid on mean here? | Make it louder | *Keep it secret or under control | Put a cover on it | Throw it away
test: What does the lid of a jar do? | Makes the jar float | Turns the jar into a bowl | Makes the jar louder | *Keeps the food fresh
exam: «A fire blanket works like a lid and takes away the oxygen.» Why does a fire blanket work like a lid? | It makes the fire hotter | It turns water into steam | It adds more fuel to the fire | *It takes away the oxygen the fire needs
